---
source: tests/snapshots.rs
expression: help_for(&args)
---
Create a POS transaction (POST /v2/pos/transactions).

Use `--wait` to long-poll until the terminal completes or rejects the transaction. Ctrl-C interrupts the create or the poll and exits 130; during the poll it prints the last-known status.

Usage: flute2 pos create [OPTIONS] --terminal-id <TERMINAL_ID> --pos-device-id <POS_DEVICE_ID> --amount <AMOUNT> --currency-code <CURRENCY_CODE>

Options:
      --terminal-id <TERMINAL_ID>
          Terminal UUID to send the transaction to (required)

      --pos-device-id <POS_DEVICE_ID>
          POS device ID (required)

      --amount <AMOUNT>
          Transaction amount (required). Plain decimal, e.g. `100.00`

      --currency-code <CURRENCY_CODE>
          Currency code, e.g. `USD` (required)

      --capture-method <CAPTURE_METHOD>
          Capture method: `auto` charges immediately, `manual` authorises for later capture
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, manual]

      --initiation-channel <INITIATION_CHANNEL>
          Initiation channel: `cloud` or `deeplink`. `deeplink` cannot be combined with `--wait`
          
          [possible values: cloud, deeplink]

      --reading-method <READING_METHOD>
          Reading method: `keyed-entry` or `regular`. Omit to let the server decide
          
          [possible values: keyed-entry, regular]

      --pricing-type <PRICING_TYPE>
          Pricing type: `card` or `cash`, for accounts with dual pricing enabled
          
          [possible values: card, cash]

      --payment-processor-id <PAYMENT_PROCESSOR_ID>
          Payment processor UUID. Defaults to the account's own

      --customer-id <CUSTOMER_ID>
          Customer UUID for vault-linked transactions

      --reference-id <REFERENCE_ID>
          Merchant-assigned reference ID, part of the duplicate-check key

      --request-storage-consent
          Ask on the terminal whether to save the payment method

      --tip-amount <TIP_AMOUNT>
          Tip amount. Plain decimal, e.g. `5.00`. At least 0.01

      --tip-rate <TIP_RATE>
          Tip rate as a percentage, e.g. `18.5` for 18.5%

      --wait
          Long-poll for terminal acceptance, then poll GET /v2/pos/transactions/{posTransactionId} every 2 seconds until the transaction leaves `InProgress` or the timeout expires

      --wait-timeout <WAIT_TIMEOUT>
          Seconds to wait for the create and the poll together before giving up (default 120, at most 86400). Requires `--wait`
          
          [default: 120]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --profile <PROFILE>
          Active profile (environment). `sandbox` (default) or `production`/`prod`
          
          [env: FLUTE2_PROFILE=]

      --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format: table (default), json, or quiet (id only). When omitted, falls back to the `FLUTE2_OUTPUT` env var, then to the `output` key in ~/.flute2/config.toml, then to `table`
          
          [env: FLUTE2_OUTPUT=]
          [possible values: table, json, quiet]

      --debug
          Print HTTP request/response traces to stderr. Card and bank-account numbers are masked to the last 4 digits; CVV/security codes are removed
